# Docker and CI

## Docker

- **Base image:** `ruby:3.3.11-slim`, multi-stage build (`Dockerfile`)
- **Node:** Node 24.x (see `.node-version`) for asset compilation
- **Yarn:** Use `yarn install --frozen-lockfile` — never modify `yarn.lock` in Docker builds
- **Assets:** Precompiled with `SECRET_KEY_BASE_DUMMY=1`
- **Runtime:** Non-root `rails` user; entrypoint at `bin/docker-entrypoint`, which runs
  `db:prepare` unless `SKIP_DB_MIGRATE=true`
- `Dockerfile.dev` is a thin dev/test image with bind-mounted source; `Dockerfile.rubocop`
  is a lint-only image with rubocop and its plugins

## docker-compose (split stacks)

Use `-f docker-compose.<stack>.yml`; each stack sets a top-level `name:` so volumes and
networks do not collide across stacks. Services run Postgres 18 and Redis 8.

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `docker-compose.dev.yml` | Local dev: Postgres + Redis + `web` + `css` watcher + `sidekiq`, app bind-mounted at `/rails`. Postgres on host port `${POSTGRES_HOST_PORT:-5442}`. `tools` profile adds `migrate`, `console`, `shell`. |
| `docker-compose.test.yml` | Tests: `prusa-print-history-dev:latest` image, bind-mounted app, cached Bundler + node_modules volumes; Postgres (tmpfs) + Redis + `test` service. |
| `docker-compose.test.build.yml` | Same as the test stack but forces a rebuild of the thin test image. |
| `docker-compose.lint.yml` | RuboCop (quick): prebuilt `prusa-print-history-rubocop:latest`, source bind-mounted at `/workspace`; no Postgres. |
| `docker-compose.lint.build.yml` | Same as the lint stack but **includes** a `build:` for `Dockerfile.rubocop`. |
| `docker-compose.server.yml` | Prod/staging-style: **no** Postgres service; set `DATABASE_URL` (or `DB_*`) for an external DB. Includes Redis for Sidekiq unless `REDIS_URL` points elsewhere. Image defaults to `ghcr.io/romkey/prusa-print-history:latest`. |

Common commands:

- **Dev stack:** `docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up`
- **Dev migrate:** `docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml --profile tools run --rm migrate`
- **Console / shell:** `docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml --profile tools run --rm console` (or `shell`)
- **Tests:** `docker compose -f docker-compose.test.yml run --rm test` — installs changed gems
  into the cached bundle volume and recreates the test DB before each run
- **A subset:** append a command, e.g.
  `docker compose -f docker-compose.test.yml run --rm test bin/rails test test/services/printer_poller_test.rb:42`
- **Tests (image rebuild):** `docker compose -f docker-compose.test.build.yml run --rm test`
- **Lint (quick):** `docker compose -f docker-compose.lint.yml run --rm rubocop` — refresh the
  image with `docker compose -f docker-compose.lint.build.yml build rubocop` when needed
- **Lint autocorrect:** `docker compose -f docker-compose.lint.yml run --rm rubocop --auto-correct`
- **Server migrate:** `docker compose -f docker-compose.server.yml --profile tools run --rm migrate`

Dev/test bind-mount the repo at `/rails`; test images must not copy application code. Lint
bind-mounts at `/workspace`; the server stack uses the built image only.

## GitHub Actions

- **ci.yml:** Runs on every push to any branch (tags excluded) and every PR. Two jobs: `lint`
  builds the RuboCop image and runs it, and `test` runs `bin/rails test` against PostgreSQL 18
  and Redis 8 service containers.
- **release.yml:** Triggered by `v*` tags; builds `linux/amd64` and `linux/arm64` images and
  pushes them to `ghcr.io/romkey/prusa-print-history` with `vX.Y.Z`, `vX.Y`, `vX`, and
  `latest` tags.
- Concurrency: `ci.yml` cancels in-progress runs for the same ref; `release.yml` does not.
